# AGENT.md — src/

Application root.

## What lives here

- `main.ts` — starts the server{{#if hasOrm}} and initializes the ORM connection{{/if}}. Nothing else.
- `app.ts` — builds the Express app and mounts every router. Import this
  directly in tests (via supertest) instead of starting a real server.
- `config/` — environment loading{{#if useSwagger}} and Swagger setup{{/if}}.
- `middlewares/` — cross-cutting request handling (errors, validation glue)
  used by more than one route.
- `shared/` — cross-cutting infrastructure (database, cache{{#if useAuth}}, auth{{/if}}{{#if useHealthCheck}}, health{{/if}}) used by more
  than one module.
- `routes/` — one directory per feature module.

## Rules

- Do not put business logic in `main.ts` or `app.ts`.
- When you add a new module, mount its router in `app.ts` in the same
  change — an unmounted router is unreachable and fails silently.
{{#if useAuth}}
- Auth middleware (`authenticate`) is imported from `shared/auth/auth.middleware`.
  Apply it as a per-route middleware in the router that needs protection.
{{/if}}
